# Ace Studio — server configuration (EXAMPLE — no real values here).
# Copy this file to `.dev.vars` for local development, or set the same
# names as secrets in your hosting dashboard for production. This is the
# only env template (the old `.dev.vars.example` was the same list, and
# is deleted). NEVER put a real key in this file, in any file the app
# serves, in a VITE_ variable, in chat, or in git. See SUPABASE_SETUP.md.
#
# --- Supabase (the backend: database + login + file storage) -------------
# Create a NEW Supabase project for Ace Studio (not the Mochris one):
# https://supabase.com/dashboard -> New project -> run
# supabase/migrations/001_ace-studio_foundation.sql in its SQL Editor.
# Then copy the values from Project Settings -> API.
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-publishable-key-here
# SECRET. Server only. Bypasses Row Level Security. Never in the browser.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key-here
#
# --- Site URL (public address — for canonical URLs + sitemap) -----------
# The public address visitors (and search/AI crawlers) use for this
# app, e.g. https://your-app-domain.example. Set it as a hosting
# secret when the app is deployed; leave it unset for local development.
# Without it, pages simply have no canonical tag yet (nothing is
# invented), and the sitemap uses the address the request came in on.
# It is also the base for password-reset links (see
# src/lib/supabase/env.ts) — never point it at another site.
# SITE_URL=https://your-app-domain.example
#
# --- Speechify (voice creation) -------------------------------------------
# How to get a key: https://platform.speechify.ai -> API Keys.
# The app's own key is used only when a visitor has not pasted their own
# session key in Settings. Leave it empty to force session keys only.
SPEECHIFY_API_KEY=
# Development-only: SPEECHIFY_MOCK=1 makes /api/narrate return a clearly
# labelled mock job (a bundled sample MP3) instead of calling Speechify,
# so the flow can be proved without a key. Never set this in production.
# SPEECHIFY_MOCK=1
#
# --- Social posting (Phase F — all optional until Kenneth connects them) --
# Each platform needs its own developer credentials. Nothing is posted
# until they are set. See src/lib/posting/CREDENTIALS.md.
# Instagram / Facebook (Meta Graph API)
# META_APP_ID=
# META_APP_SECRET=
# IG_USER_ID=
# IG_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# FACEBOOK_PAGE_ID=
# FACEBOOK_PAGE_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# TikTok (Content Posting API)
# TIKTOK_CLIENT_KEY=
# TIKTOK_CLIENT_SECRET=
# TIKTOK_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# YouTube (Data API v3, OAuth2)
# YOUTUBE_CLIENT_ID=
# YOUTUBE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# YOUTUBE_REFRESH_TOKEN=
